# Supabase MCP — use the "test" branch

When calling Supabase MCP tools that require a `project_id`/project ref
(`execute_sql`, `apply_migration`, `list_tables`, `get_advisors`, etc.), target
the **`test`** development branch, never the default `main` branch.

- **test branch** (USE THIS): project ref `wzcppuywyisfhjxaejld`
- **main / default** (DO NOT USE for writes/queries): `mhlmbpnyckrqyznwmbwo`

Branch refs can change if a branch is recreated. If a call fails or the ref
looks stale, re-run `list_branches` with `project_id: "mhlmbpnyckrqyznwmbwo"`
(the parent project) and pick the branch named `test`.

Only use `main` if the user explicitly asks for production/main.
